---
title: GitHub lifecycle DAG (dag_workflow.py) — states and entrypoints
---
stateDiagram-v2
    %% Source of truth: .agents/hooks/dag_workflow.py DAG (lines 46-52).
    %% Transitions carry the wrapper scripts/skills that advance the state;
    %% raw git/gh commands are blocked by github_command_guard.

    state start_fork <<fork>>
    state pr_join <<join>>
    state gates_fork <<fork>>
    state merge_join <<join>>

    [*] --> start_fork: start_task skill
    start_fork --> issue_created
    start_fork --> branch_created

    issue_created: issue.created
    branch_created: branch.created
    branch_pushed: branch.pushed
    pr_opened: pr.opened
    ci_green: ci.green
    review_approved: review.approved
    pr_merged: pr.merged

    branch_created --> branch_pushed: push_branch.sh
    issue_created --> pr_join
    branch_pushed --> pr_join
    pr_join --> pr_opened: draft PR (start_task /\ncreate_nojira_pr.sh)

    pr_opened --> gates_fork: promote_review.sh /\nfinish_pr.sh
    gates_fork --> ci_green: CI workflows pass
    gates_fork --> review_approved: review cycles\n(monitor_pr.sh --review-cycle N)
    ci_green --> merge_join
    review_approved --> merge_join
    merge_join --> pr_merged: monitor_pr.sh --merge /\nfinish_pr.sh
    pr_merged --> [*]

    note right of pr_opened
        Iterate freely before the gates:
        edit, test, push_branch.sh.
        The DAG guard only fires on
        push / PR create / ready / merge.
    end note
